Subject: [PATCH 11/22] Decode attention: G6_ATTN_SC2 (scores_sc, S slots per
 warp) + G6_ATTN_CTX2 (context PB / packed / E1 PART 32), default off; attnk
 bench

scores_sc<S,TR>: scores_heads<16> with S consecutive slots per warp, head loop unrolled, each head's
query loaded once for S slots; per (row, head, slot) the same fmaf chain, warp_sum (or scores_tr's
transpose reduction with G6_ATTN_SC2_TR=1), scale and -inf -> bit-identical scores.
G6_ATTN_CTX2=1/2: context_parts_heads with 32/64 gathered pairs per batch; 3/4: context_pk (slot-major
probabilities, select instead of skip branches, two register batches in flight) -> bit-identical parts.
G6_ATTN_CTX2=9 (E1): context_pk over 32 partitions of 64 slots + merge_parts over 32 partials.
Flags unset: the stock kernels (same SASS), the same workspace layout.
tests/attnk.cu: stock vs each arm on the replayed decode chain (byte compares of raw scores, parts,
probs, context, outputs, indices, kv; per-node and whole-call hot/cold timing; per-step projection).
